                <pb facs="0750" n="744" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg744"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to the Earl of Rosebery.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic">May 17,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to acquaint your
                    lordship, in accordance with telegraphic instructions from the Secretary of
                    State, that my Government accepts the extension of the Samoan land commission
                    until March 31, 1894, the German Government having agreed to do likewise, and
                    that a new American commissioner will at once he appointed in the place of Mr.
                    Ormshee, who has resigned.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
